46edd59fb1c26372db042e230f9d2d3ec5a4e08d329361","taskId":"container-recipe"},{"mergeCommit":"e4ac78a9ba2a84aca3baec47a4698602a2f3b850","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f","revision":"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b","taskId":"instruments"},{"mergeCommit":"b474021c40d16a6bd0fce9ac2b9002b4e6538cc4","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f","revision":"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d","taskId":"host-tooling"},{"mergeCommit":"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa","pullRequest":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9","revision":"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225","taskId":"bench-harness"}],"checkpoints":[],"remaining":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package","cp-weights","cp-build","cp-smoke","cp-proxy","cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close"],"frontier":["proxy-tooling"],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/9","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains because the attempt left head identical to the prepared base 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, so no task work existed to validate. Evidence: the captured diff is empty (head == baseRev, empty patch), the driver reported \"spec-build-driver: agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\", and the worktree is clean with docs/ still holding only GATE0.md and CONTINGENCY-sampler-cu-remaining-1024-launches.patch — no docs/MORNING.md and no docs/ANNOUNCE.md. The accompanying result-projection-timeout on the finalMessage capture is a downstream symptom of the attempt ending without a committed result, not an independent machinery fault, so this is not transient; the missing deliverables are both inside the authorized docs prefix, so it is not blocked either. Attempt 2 steering: (1) read specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6 and #r7, IMPORTS.md, and README.md for style before writing; (2) create docs/MORNING.md carrying the five required sections with those literal headings — \"Receipt review\" (one row per receipt under results/receipts with status and the bound it was graded against), \"Open items\" (every spec UNKNOWN with its drain state), \"Promotion checklist\" (operator verification before any fleet change, per ruling P13), \"Optimization menu\" (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md), and a blocker template implementing ruling P16 that uses the word \"blocker\"; (3) create a non-empty docs/ANNOUNCE.md covering the two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire, what was built overnight, where evidence lives, and where benchmarks land; (4) run the ledger-sections acceptance argv locally and see it pass; (5) git add only paths under docs/, commit, and confirm git status --porcelain prints nothing before finishing. Committing is the deliverable — an uncommitted working tree reproduces this exact failure.","taskId":"morning-ledger","verdict":"retry"}],"retries":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/10","reason":"Stage `ownership` faulted.\n\nThe judge classified this failure as transient.\n\nTerminated the spec-build-driver worker session before it produced any file, envelope, or commit, so the ownership gate conflict-domains failed on a pristine lane rather than on any defect in the task's work. Evidence for a session/machinery fault rather than a worker fault: the recorded adapter error is result-projection-timeout — the configured finalMessage capture for adapter spec-build-driver was not projected within 10000 ms with exitEvidencePassed false — meaning no worker envelope of any kind (completion, needs-authority, or impossible) ever reached the driver, and the gate's own stderr 'agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base' is the downstream consequence. Independent inspection of the assigned worktree confirms the lane is untouched at the prepared base 71f2beb: `git status --porcelain` is empty, `git status --porcelain --ignored` is empty (no untracked or ignored residue), the stash is empty, the reflog's only entries are the preparation 'reset: moving to HEAD', and every path in the tree carries the identical worktree-creation mtime of 12:35:48. scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh were never created and results/receipts/proxy.json is absent, so the diff is empty with head == baseRev. This is specifically NOT the uncommitted-work trap that overseer steering comment 7 anticipated: that failure mode leaves modified or untracked files behind in the lane, and none exist here. Consequently there is no actionable in-domain fix to convert into attempt-2 steering, which rules out retry; and there is no missing authority, dependency, gate-contract defect, or out-of-task source fix — the declared conflict domains scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, tests are sufficient for the stated goal (the receipt path results/receipts/proxy.json sits under an already-tracked results/receipts directory) — which rules out blocked. The correct disposition is a machin...","taskId":"proxy-tooling"},{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/5","reason":"Stage `ownership` faulted.\n\nThe judge classified this failure as transient.\n\nAborted before the worker committed anything, so the ownership gate \"conflict-domains\" failed on an empty change set rather than on a boundary violation. Evidence: diff.head equals baseRev 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa with an empty patch; the lane worktree is clean (git status --porcelain empty, docs/ still holds only the pre-existing GATE0.md, CONTINGENCY patch, and .gitkeep), so no partial or uncommitted task work exists to preserve. The recorded cause is adapter-side: result-schema-mismatch wrapping result-projection-timeout, where the configured finalMessage capture for adapter \"spec-build-driver\" was not projected within 10000 ms and exitEvidencePassed was false; stderr \"spec-build-driver: agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\" is the downstream consequence of that lost session, not an independent implementation finding. Nothing in the record implicates the task definition: the goal writes only docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the binding conflictDomains prefix [\"docs\"], the single acceptance criterion ledger-sections is satisfiable entirely within that prefix, and both dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are already merged into the prepared base as commits b474021 and 71f2beb. There is no needs-authority envelope, no workerOutcomeClaim, no steering, and no prior diagnosis, so there is no substantive defect for attempt-2 steering to correct and no out-of-task authority or gate-contract change to propose. This is a harness or session fault that should consume the bounded machinery-retry budget: re-dispatch the same task revision sha256:4c0b640cab49ea7ac3b57b4e23f66c726b92fcce08e77d0f8816814181c3ba0a unchanged on the same lane so the driver can capture a final message and land a commit.","taskId":"morning-ledger"}],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[{"taskId":"cp-weights","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-build","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-smoke","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-proxy","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-tp2","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-bench","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-close","waitingOn":["rdma-package"]}],"blocked":[],"quiescent":false,"escalation":null,"closingSummary":null,"warnings":[]},"maintenance":{"blockingJobs":[],"cleaned":["pass:/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/.state/passes/041c26c3e366.json"],"currentRunHash":"8b393a90cca3","liveRuns":[],"warnings":[]},"checkpoints":[],"merged":[],"published":null,"failures":[{"taskId":"proxy-tooling","stage":"ownership","verdict":"failed","detail":"{\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"projection\":{\"code\":\"result-projection-timeout\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"adapter\":\"spec-build-driver\",\"attempt\":1,\"taskUuid\":\"01a04d18-b628-7ae0-a1e7-f69b0c011dae\",\"timeoutMs\":10000,\"exitEvidencePassed\":false}}}}"}],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"blocked":false,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/11","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"redacted":false,"retry":null,"taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"retry"}],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"continuation":{"created":true,"dedupKey":"campaign-continuation:mecattaf/flashnext:1:continuation-650fffe1783fd57d68095d799ae2dd49","event":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/events/campaign-continuation-7ddaddb23af10557fb22f04f5360c55f.json","receipt":"local://mecattaf/flashnext/refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/continuation/continuation-650fffe1783fd57d68095d799ae2dd49","runId":"continuation-650fffe1783fd57d68095d799ae2dd49"},"escalation":null}}}
